{
  "title": "Server small dedupes: AI client construction, shared SQL function \
declarations, export.rs split",
  "description": "Three small, independent server cleanups:\n\
\n\
1. AI client construction + error mapping is copy-pasted and inconsistent: \
CachingAiClient::from_env() with an identical Err -> service_unavailable(\"AI \
service unavailable\") arm appears in api/enrich.rs:103,182, \
api/recipes/normalize_title.rs:153, api/recipes/generate_description.rs:161, \
while api/recipes/generate_photo.rs:202 uses a different entry point \
(AiConfig::from_env). Add one helper ai_client_from_env() -> Result<_, \
ApiError> used by all AI endpoints.\n\
\n\
2. Duplicated define_sql_function! declarations: lower() is declared \
independently in api/recipes/list.rs:33-36 and api/public/auth/login.rs:11; \
list.rs also declares cardinality and random (list.rs:23-31). Move shared \
Postgres function declarations into raw_sql.rs (or a sql_functions module) and \
import.\n\
\n\
3. api/recipes/export.rs (564 lines) mixes Paprika format conversion \
(convert_to_paprika:73, PaprikaRecipe/PaprikaPhoto structs), gzip/zip \
streaming plumbing (ChannelWriter:381, write_zip_stream:412), photo fetching \
(fetch_recipe_photos:198), and two handlers. Extract paprika.rs (format model \
+ conversion) and zip_stream.rs; leave handlers thin.\n\
\n\
All behavior-preserving; no client changes, no pipeline data/ diffs expected.",
